[Unit]
Description=QuantOS candidate 20 (Good Night scalper) real at-open window liquidity probe (read-only, no orders)
After=network-online.target
Wants=network-online.target

[Service]
Type=oneshot
User=ubuntu
WorkingDirectory=/home/ubuntu/quantos
ExecStart=/home/ubuntu/quantos/.venv/bin/python /home/ubuntu/quantos/scripts/probe_goodnight_openwindow.py
Environment=HOME=/home/ubuntu

# Recurring daily feasibility-gathering job (converted 2026-09-04 from a
# one-time 3x-same-day design -- see the .timer for why) -- still not a
# production/execution job, still read-only, no orders. Accumulates one
# real at-open reading per trading morning into data_cache/goodnight_
# openwindow_probe.csv until there's enough to actually decide anything
# about candidate 20's liquidity (user's own framing: "gather a few more
# at-open sessions" before drawing a conclusion, 2026-09-04).
#
# Depends on the VM's Fyers token already being freshly refreshed before
# 09:16 IST -- same daily manual (now dashboard-assisted, see
# [[quantos_dashboard_fyers_token_refresh]]) refresh every other morning
# job here relies on. A stale token fails this run harmlessly (no
# orders, self-healing: just misses that day's sample).
#
# No market-hours ExecCondition here (unlike quantos-orb-spread-probe.
# service/quantos-orb-stopout-probe.service, which fire many times across
# a whole session): this is a single well-timed daily fire, and a holiday
# or off-hours miss just produces an empty/harmless run, same tolerance
# already disclosed in the probe script's own docstring.
